%% NER off the event loop: only DETECTION by a model moves to a worker
%% thread; the redaction itself stays synchronous (one vault transaction).
%% Code: src/llm_redact/ner_prefetch.py, detection/engine.py (DetectorPlan,
%% FairLock), redactor.py (with_precomputed). Docs: docs/how-it-works.md.
%% Render: scripts/render_diagrams.sh (PNG committed next to this source).
%% animate: the messages appear in order; scripts/animate_diagrams.py renders the
%% animated SVG + GIF committed next to this source (a '%% animate' marker opts in).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant E as Event loop (proxy)
    participant W as NER worker thread
    participant N as NER model<br/>(one lock per model)
    participant V as Vault (local)

    Note over E: a JSON body, an upload or a realtime frame
    E->>E: collecting pass: run the request's own redaction<br/>with a stand-in that only records the strings
    E->>W: prefetch(unique strings)<br/>— one request's batch at a time
    Note over E: free: other requests are answered meanwhile
    loop each string
        W->>N: take the lock, detect ONE string, release
        N-->>W: raw detections
    end
    W-->>E: table: string → each model's detections
    E->>E: synchronous redaction: regex rules + deny strings run,<br/>NER results come from the table
    opt a string missing from the table (or a reload swapped the detectors)
        E->>N: detect it inline, under the same lock — first come, first<br/>served: waits for at most the string the worker is on
        N-->>E: detections (counted: prefetch_misses, inline_calls)
    end
    E->>V: new values → tokens, one transaction (no await inside)
    V-->>E: «PERSON_001» …
    Note over E,V: The outcome never depends on the table: it only moves where the models run.
